From: hybrid-reasoner debug session 2026-06-02
Subject: cut gen sidecar over to gen_sidecar_launcher (memory watchdog)

The 2026-06-02 incident showed the gen sidecar (mlx_lm.server) growing to
36 GB with zero memory cap, because mlx_lm.server is a third-party Python
entry point and never calls apply_boot_guards.

src/gen_sidecar_launcher.py wraps it as a child process and watchdogs its
phys_footprint via _phys_footprint_darwin(pid). On cap-exceeded the child
gets SIGKILL and the launcher exits 75 so the supervisor restarts it.

These two files are guarded; apply with RC_ALLOW_GUARD_EDIT=1 in your shell.

Apply with:
  RC_ALLOW_GUARD_EDIT=1 git apply scripts/gen-sidecar-cutover.patch

--- a/src/sidecar_supervisor.py
+++ b/src/sidecar_supervisor.py
@@ -186,7 +186,11 @@ def _build_children(repo_root: Path) -> List[_Child]:
         # returns 200 once the model is loaded. Works on llama_cpp.server too.
         children.append(_Child(
             name="gen",
-            cmd=["bash", str(repo_root / "scripts" / "start-gen-sidecar.sh")],
+            # Route through gen_sidecar_launcher so MLX / Metal allocations
+            # are watchdogged against S2_GEN_MEM_LIMIT_GB (falls back to
+            # S2_MEM_LIMIT_GB). Shell script kept as a manual entry point but
+            # no longer the supervisor-managed path. 2026-06-02 incident fix.
+            cmd=[sys.executable, "-m", "gen_sidecar_launcher"],
             health_url=f"http://127.0.0.1:{gen_port}/v1/models",
         ))
     return children
